---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
const lastUpdated = "August 10, 2026";
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How The Digital Income Edit™ collects, uses, and protects your information."
>
  <div class="page-eyebrow">Legal</div>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

  <p>The Digital Income Edit™ ("we," "us," "our") operates www.thedigitalincomeedit.com and its related educational content, community, and product offerings. This policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have.</p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We collect information in the following ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Information you provide directly</strong> — your name and email address when you subscribe to our newsletter, download a free resource, join our community, or purchase a product.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment information</strong> — processed by our third-party payment providers. We do not store your full payment card details on our servers.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data</strong> — collected automatically through analytics, including pages visited, time on site, and general location and device information.</li>
    <li><strong>Third-party platform data</strong> — where you connect or interact with us through a third-party platform such as Pinterest, we may receive information made available through that platform's API, limited to what is necessary to provide the service you have requested.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To deliver the content, resources, or products you have requested</li>
    <li>To send newsletters, updates, and communications you have opted into</li>
    <li>To operate, maintain, and improve our website and services</li>
    <li>To process purchases and manage membership access</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How We Share Your Information</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share information only with the service providers required to operate our business — including our email platform, payment processors, and community hosting platform — and only to the extent needed for them to perform their function.</p>

  <h2>Third-Party Platforms</h2>
  <p>Our website and business may link to or integrate with third-party platforms, including Pinterest. When you interact with these platforms, their own privacy policies govern how they handle your information. Any data we access through a connected platform's API is used solely to operate the feature you have engaged with, and is not shared with unrelated third parties.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use cookies and similar technologies to understand how visitors use our site and to support essential site functionality. You can control cookies through your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>Your Choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You may unsubscribe from marketing emails at any time using the link in any email we send.</li>
    <li>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information by contacting us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data Security</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable measures to protect your information, but no method of transmission or storage is completely secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>Our services are not directed to individuals under 18, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.</p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or your information can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@thedigitalincomeedit.com" style="color:var(--pink);font-weight:500">hello@thedigitalincomeedit.com</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
